  "description": "This slide introduces the concept of internal goods movements in SAP Extended Warehouse Management (EWM). Internal goods movements pertain to the physical relocation of stock within a warehouse, without altering stock ownership or type. These movements are critical for optimizing space utilization, enhancing accessibility, and ensuring seamless warehouse operations. Types of internal movements include: \n\n- **Replenishment:** Transferring stock from main storage areas to pick locations for easier access.\n- **Bin-to-bin transfer:** Shifting handling units between bins within the same storage type.\n- **Ad-hoc movements:** Conducting manual or unplanned stock relocations based on immediate operational demands.\n- **Posting changes:** Modifying stock due to quality inspections or other adjustments."
}
```

