  "title": "Comprehensive Guide to Make to Order (MTO) and Production Order Management Processes",
  "description": {
    "overview": "This document provides an in-depth overview of the Make to Order (MTO) production process and the end-to-end workflow for managing and executing production orders within the 'Produce to Supply' (P2S) framework, as implemented by Bosch Rexroth AG. The MTO strategy focuses on manufacturing goods for specific customer sales orders, enabling high customization, efficient production, and reduced inventory costs. The production order management process ensures seamless execution, traceability, and accurate cost tracking for customer-specific manufacturing.",
    "keyTopics": [
      {
        "topic": "Make to Order (MTO) Process",
        "details": [
          "Definition and benefits of MTO, including reduced inventory costs, enhanced customer satisfaction, and flexible market responses.",
          "Examples of MTO products: conveyor systems, customizable hydraulic valves, multi-axis systems, and advanced motion control drive units.",
          "Prerequisites for MTO production: sales order creation, material master configuration, and Material Requirements Planning (MRP).",
          "Step-by-step guide to MTO execution: planned order conversion, sequencing, production order release, confirmations, and goods delivery.",
          "Key system statuses: CRTD (Created), REL (Released), MACM (Material Committed), MSPT (Missing Parts).",
          "Integration of Sales and Distribution (SD), Production Planning (PP), and Controlling (CO) for seamless operations."
        ]
      },
      {
        "topic": "Production Order Management and Execution",
        "details": [
          "Release of production orders via MD04 (manual) or COHV (mass processing), with system statuses transitioning from CRTD to REL.",
